 the collision, the employee signaled for the other driver to pull into a nearby convenience store parking lot. At that point, the third party fled the scene. The employee contacted 911, and three witnesses pursued the fleeing driver, successfully stopping and detaining them until law enforcement arrived.\n\nLocal police responded to the scene, gathered the necessary information from the employee, and released him shortly thereafter. The employee was unable to obtain any information from the other driver. No citations were issued to the employee, and no medical attention was required.\n\nAt this time, it is unknown what actions law enforcement took regarding the third party. The official crash report is not yet available. Case File #26006345 was provided at the scene.","location":"Intersection of Hwy 385 and Truck Route 1910, Andrews TX","service_line":"Hutch's Oilfield Supply","company":"Hutchs Oilfield Supply and Equipment LLC","report_number":"78008536"}],"assessments":{"total":13,"details":[{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"James Stone","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78041037"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Arturo Cerda","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78040737"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78039369"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78038899"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78037902"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Roger Gray","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"77998793"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"77990984"},{"date":"2026-03-27","assessor":"Laredo Dispatch","form_id":229645,"division":"Casing","location":"